(575349, 58359, 14476, '<td valign="top">Ellamay, I am delighted to see all the positive comments on your wonderful entry.  Keep up the good, and original, work.  Your beautiful beastie is now one of my "Favorites."</td>', 'Ellamay, I am delighted to see all the positive comments on your wonderful entry.  Keep up the good, and original, work.  Your beautiful beastie is now one of my "Favorites."', '2004-02-11 00:22:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(575350, 57471, 16499, '<td valign="top">From critique club.<br/> <br/>I agree with the resto of the commenters - the color composition that can not go wrong and fine composition. The reflection which is as perfect as image represents the title in full. I rated it among the best images for this challenge.<br/> <br/>What annoys me a bit is some perspective distorsion at the top-left and the DOF which covers only 1/3 of the image in the middle. I''d love the top and bottom sharper.<br/> <br/>There is another though regarding color. The whole image consists of two tones, yet at the bottom-right we see a bright hilite. It would be aceptable if the image revealed some of the stainless steel gray - may be a little of the white light from the left... Or, otherwise - the hilite was dimmed a bit.</td>', 'From critique club. I agree with the resto of the commenters - the color composition that can not go wrong and fine composition. The reflection which is as perfect as image represents the title in full. I rated it among the best images for this challenge. What annoys me a bit is some perspective distorsion at the top-left and the DOF which covers only 1/3 of the image in the middle. I''d love the top and bottom sharper. There is another though regarding color. The whole image consists of two tones, yet at the bottom-right we see a bright hilite. It would be aceptable if the image revealed some of the stainless steel gray - may be a little of the white light from the left... Or, otherwise - the hilite was dimmed a bit.', '2004-02-11 00:22:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(575356, 57871, 327, '<td valign="top">Twice you cleaned that driveway! <b>DPC Dedication</b> <br/>Totally fun shot.</td>', 'Twice you cleaned that driveway! DPC Dedication Totally fun shot.', '2004-02-11 00:23:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(575357, 57911, 15305, '<td valign="top">Congratulations on your ribbon. I was sure this would be one of the top three.</td>', 'Congratulations on your ribbon. I was sure this would be one of the top three.', '2004-02-11 00:23:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(575361, 58359, 14499, '<td valign="top">Yes, It should have ranked higher for the originality, I loved it too!</td>', 'Yes, It should have ranked higher for the originality, I loved it too!', '2004-02-11 00:23:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(575366, 57897, 15305, '<td valign="top">I really thought this one would be one of the best three.... Anyway, it''s in the top ten. Congratulations.</td>', 'I really thought this one would be one of the best three.... Anyway, it''s in the top ten. Congratulations.', '2004-02-11 00:26:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(575389, 57673, 16703, '<td valign="top">i am sorry that you got a rather low place, i thought your picture was up there and it was my most favorite pick...</td>', 'i am sorry that you got a rather low place, i thought your picture was up there and it was my most favorite pick...', '2004-02-11 00:32:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(575394, 58542, 16499, '<td valign="top">From critique club.<br/> <br/>Tyler, I am looking at your works for the third time now and realize that you are a master of mood. In this case everything - sepia, grain, items in the frame and composition prove that tis is really forgotten corner.<br/> <br/>My problem is that I dont like myself in the mood which your photo casts on me. I hate such corners - I''ve seen them too much. And watching your work does not leave me any optimism and hope. This is definitely art, but I gave it only +4 because I can not live with such entropy...</td>', 'From critique club. Tyler, I am looking at your works for the third time now and realize that you are a master of mood. In this case everything - sepia, grain, items in the frame and composition prove that tis is really forgotten corner. My problem is that I dont like myself in the mood which your photo casts on me. I hate such corners - I''ve seen them too much. And watching your work does not leave me any optimism and hope. This is definitely art, but I gave it only +4 because I can not live with such entropy...', '2004-02-11 00:34:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(575398, 57937, 14499, '<td valign="top">This apears to be a XR6 Ford Falcon (all Ozzie built) but I will let Jarrad confirm that for you.<br/> <br/><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by scrum8:</b></div><hr/><i> Is that a Mustang? The first time I looked I thought it was, but I wasn''t sure on the 2nd look. Anyway, my plant starts building the 2005 Stang in September. Nice effect with the backlighting and the use of headlamps. </i></td></tr></table></td>', 'This apears to be a XR6 Ford Falcon (all Ozzie built) but I will let Jarrad confirm that for you. Originally posted by scrum8: Is that a Mustang? The first time I looked I thought it was, but I wasn''t sure on the 2nd look. Anyway, my plant starts building the 2005 Stang in September. Nice effect with the backlighting and the use of headlamps. ', '2004-02-11 00:35:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(575418, 57687, 16499, '<td valign="top">From critique club.<br/> <br/>As I said before - it''s little off-focus, but I still gave it a good mark.<br/> <br/>I was just thinking... The spark has to be blueish in the air and the electrodes would cast some shadows - that will change the spark shape from round to elliptical. There is some color in the spark - which is nice. Also the tone of zink coating is very realistic.</td>', 'From critique club. As I said before - it''s little off-focus, but I still gave it a good mark. I was just thinking... The spark has to be blueish in the air and the electrodes would cast some shadows - that will change the spark shape from round to elliptical. There is some color in the spark - which is nice. Also the tone of zink coating is very realistic.', '2004-02-11 00:43:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(575419, 58523, 5515, '<td valign="top">What an incredibly original thought. Just wonderous. Congrats... dave</td>', 'What an incredibly original thought. Just wonderous. Congrats... dave', '2004-02-11 00:44:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(575425, 57851, 12131, '<td valign="top">I actually think this is a creative shot.  You help heighten the flower by cutting the frame in the same direction.  I think you should have scored much higher, because really, you did artwork from garage type stuff.  It''s literally garage art and that is far more than many in this challenge did. Perhaps if the branches were moved aside that would help.</td>', 'I actually think this is a creative shot.  You help heighten the flower by cutting the frame in the same direction.  I think you should have scored much higher, because really, you did artwork from garage type stuff.  It''s literally garage art and that is far more than many in this challenge did. Perhaps if the branches were moved aside that would help.', '2004-02-11 00:45:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(575451, 58416, 7151, '<td valign="top">Guess that new G5 paid off:  1 challenge, 1 ribbon.  :)  Too bad my Shallow DOF entry won''t follow suit.  :(<br/> <br/>Thanks to everyone who voted and took time to comment.</td>', 'Guess that new G5 paid off:  1 challenge, 1 ribbon.  :)  Too bad my Shallow DOF entry won''t follow suit.  :( Thanks to everyone who voted and took time to comment.', '2004-02-11 00:54:00.000000', NULL, 0),
